"1. Pediatr Infect Dis J. 2017 Oct;36(10):973-975. doi: \n10.1097/INF.0000000000001639.\n\nPharmaceutical Dosing Errors at a Pediatric HIV Clinic in Mwanza, Tanzania.\n\nNaik NM(1), Mbwanji RN, Mgawe M, Ongoa R, Gesase AE, Schutze GE, Minde M, Mwita \nLF.\n\nAuthor information:\n(1)From the *Department of Pediatrics, Baylor College of Medicine, Houston, \nTexas; and \u2020Baylor College of Medicine Children's Foundation - Tanzania, \nPaediatrics, Mwanza, Tanzania.\n\nThe outpatient medication dosing error rate at a pediatric HIV clinic in Mwanza, \nTanzania, was about 1 in every 34 prescriptions. Young children were at highest \nrisk of a dosing error likely because of dose changes with growth and also the \ninconsistent supply of pediatric formulations. Majority of errors occurred at \nconsecutive visits suggesting clinicians reordered medication without double \nchecking dosing.\n\nDOI: 10.1097/INF.0000000000001639\nPMID: 28498304 [Indexed for MEDLINE]"